# The build context, kept to what the image actually needs.
#
# Without this the context is ~everything: a local .venv, a Rust target
# directory that can reach a gigabyte, every reports-* directory from every
# past run, and the whole of .git. Worst of all it would sweep in vendor/ --
# so a CI leg that had just fetched one vendor's installer would ship it to
# the daemon while building a different vendor's image.
.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
server/target/
reports/
reports-*/
site/
columns/
*.html
